        "header": "2Model Design",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.03796/2609.03796v1/llada_image_arch.png",
                "caption": "Figure 3:Overview of the LLaDA-Image architecture.Learnable query tokens aggregate information from the input tokens through\ncross-attention in the RQA. The resulting query representations are\nconcatenated with the original inputs and encoded by LLaDA 2.0 Mini, after\nwhich the connector maps the hidden states into the DiT conditioning\nspace. The FLUX.2 VAE supplies image latents, while editing additionally\nconditions the generator on SigLIP-VQ features and clean VAE latents from\nthe reference image. All modal tokens are concatenated and processed by\nthe single-stream DiT to predict the flow-matching velocity.",
                "position": 874
            }
        ]
    },
